# Module 36 – HI-TECH College Website Chatbot & AI Support Centre

This module adds a website chatbot that can answer prospective students' questions, explain courses and admissions, guide applicants through the application process, and direct existing students to the correct portal.

It will have two operating modes:

- Knowledge-based support: answers from approved college information stored in the database.
- AI-assisted support: uses a configured AI provider to generate responses grounded in approved college information.

The chatbot must not invent fee amounts, admission decisions, examination results or payment confirmations. It should refer uncertain or personal-account questions to the appropriate college office.

## 1. Chatbot features

| Feature               | Description                                             |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Welcome message       | Introduces HI-TECH College and support options          |
| Course enquiries      | Explains approved courses and programmes                |
| Admissions            | Application requirements and application links          |
| Fees                  | Answers from approved fee structures                    |
| Student portal        | Guides students to portal login and password recovery   |
| Staff support         | Directs staff to staff portal                           |
| Examination support   | Explains exam procedures and timetables                 |
| Library support       | Guides users to library services                        |
| Contact support       | Provides approved office contacts                       |
| Live support requests | Captures a user's request for staff follow-up           |
| Knowledge base        | Uses approved college FAQ articles                      |
| Conversation history  | Stores conversations with privacy controls              |
| Escalation            | Transfers unanswered questions to a human support queue |
| Analytics             | Tracks common questions and unresolved enquiries        |
| Mobile support        | Responsive floating chat interface                      |

## 2. Database models

Add the following to `apps/api/prisma/schema.prisma`. Check for existing chatbot or support-ticket models before adding duplicates.

```
enum ChatbotMessageRole {
  USER
  ASSISTANT
  SYSTEM
}

enum ChatbotConversationStatus {
  OPEN
  ESCALATED
  CLOSED
}

enum ChatbotKnowledgeStatus {
  DRAFT
  PUBLISHED
  ARCHIVED
}

enum ChatbotEscalationStatus {
  PENDING
  ASSIGNED
  RESOLVED
  REJECTED
}

model ChatbotConversation {
  id            String   @id @default(cuid())
  institutionId String
  sessionId     String
  userId        String?
  visitorName   String?
  visitorEmail  String?
  status        ChatbotConversationStatus @default(OPEN)
  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt     DateTime @updatedAt
  messages      ChatbotMessage[]
  escalation   ChatbotEscalation?

  @@index([institutionId, sessionId])
  @@index([institutionId, status, createdAt])
  @@index([userId])
}

model ChatbotMessage {
  id             String   @id @default(cuid())
  conversationId String
  role           ChatbotMessageRole
  content        String   @db.Text
  source          String?
  createdAt       DateTime @default(now())

  conversation ChatbotConversation @relation(
    fields: [conversationId],
    references: [id],
    onDelete: Cascade
  )

  @@index([conversationId, createdAt])
}

model ChatbotKnowledgeArticle {
  id            String   @id @default(cuid())
  institutionId String
  category      String
  question      String
  answer        String   @db.Text
  keywords      String[]
  status        ChatbotKnowledgeStatus @default(DRAFT)
  displayOrder  Int      @default(0)
  createdById   String
  updatedById   String?
  createdAt     DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt     DateTime @updatedAt

  @@index([institutionId, status, category])
}

model ChatbotEscalation {
  id             String   @id @default(cuid())
  conversationId String   @unique
  institutionId  String
  assignedToId   String?
  subject        String
  department     String
  description    String   @db.Text
  status         ChatbotEscalationStatus @default(PENDING)
  resolution     String?  @db.Text
  createdAt      DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt      DateTime @updatedAt

  conversation ChatbotConversation @relation(
    fields: [conversationId],
    references: [id],
    onDelete: Cascade
  )

  @@index([institutionId, status, createdAt])
  @@index([assignedToId])
}
```

