Only publish information verified by the relevant college office. In particular, Finance should approve fee information, Registrar should approve admissions requirements, and the Academic Office should approve course information.

## 11. Important corrections before testing

There are three implementation details to address:

A. Prevent the AI from answering without approved knowledge.

In `collegeChatbot.ts`, replace:

```
const aiAnswer = await generateChatbotAnswer({ messages });
```

with:

```
const aiAnswer = knowledge.length > 0
  ? await generateChatbotAnswer({ messages })
  : null;
```

This ensures the AI is not asked to answer questions without any matching approved college information.

B. Fix Express route ordering.

In `chatbotAdmin.ts`, register:

```
router.patch("/escalations/:id", ...);
```

before any generic parameter routes if you add them later. Also, in `websiteNavigation.ts`, move the `/reorder` route above `PATCH /:id` so it is not interpreted as an item ID.

C. Validate the conversation session.

A browser-generated UUID is not sufficient authentication for accessing sensitive records. The public API should use rate limits, origin restrictions, abuse protection and a proper session ownership mechanism. Do not expose private student records through the chatbot.

